From 12c55a285f94e7171e4a0efb4a9c50a10a1eb54d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:01:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Start edge wear only at exposed creases and chip its
 boundary

Root cause of the owner's crate defects: crease spans buried inside other
parts (body edges inside the posts, band corners) were wear sources, and the
baker read other parts hidden just behind a surface as convex edges (dashes
on the posts). Natural spread now keeps only exposed crease spans (per-part
inside test, overlapping solids tested separately), the baker ignores
foreign surfaces behind the tangent plane, and a finer Pattern-size field
chips the boundary so narrow bands are no longer straight stripes.

Adds a CPU crate render example and numeric regressions for buried sources,
fake post dashes, owner Level 0.065 / Spread 12.5 reach and boundary detail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
