From 89d9ae99720fdc00c17b7044822b6e4118f7766d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:07:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Unfold wrapped brush dabs across hard edges instead of
 smearing them

Tangent | Wrap mapped side-face texels by radial 3D distance, which barely
grows just past an edge, so textured tips smeared into a fan down the side.
Footprints now lay each texel's face flat onto the stamp plane about the
line where the planes meet, preserving surface distance across folds (exact
for hard edges; bounded on bevels). Planar, camera and UV modes unchanged;
the shared kernel coverage applies to paint, masks and Paint effects.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SABuzavAnWVt61Gj6ugyYB
