From 1420a6a9a107ec10d506f5f3f18614e62c108bfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:23:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Activate Shelf brushes in one click with a fading
 viewport notice

A single click on a Shelf brush or tip now applies it through one app call
(Session::select_shelf_brush), switches Fill/Eyedropper/Pen to the Brush,
leaves picking mode and keeps the content/mask/Paint-effect destination.
A brief 'Brush: name' plate with the tip thumbnail appears inside the 3D
view's top-left corner, then fades. Double-click brings the Brush settings
tab forward instead of re-selecting. Tip clicks no longer open a preview
popup. Failed presets report in the status bar and show no notice.

Adds --select-brush for scripted native captures, plus state, real egui
click/double-click, notice placement/fade and dock-focus tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SABuzavAnWVt61Gj6ugyYB
